Given all inputs and properties tables set-up:
Assume ambient temp is 298K, then T_co = T_amb (non cryogenic)

AREA LOOP (dp optimization)
(move channel geometry here)

    PRESSURE LOOP
    Set P_guess

        AXIAL MARCH
        FOR dx in no. geometric stations:
            Solve for v using mdot equation -> v = mdot_f / rho * Aw_cool
            Find Reynolds number based on local rho, v, Dh, mu
            Find Prandtl using local Cp, mu, k
            Find Nusselt with Gnielinski
            Find coolant convection HT coeff h_c = Nu * k / Dh

            HOT WALL TEMP SOLVE
            t_w_guess = value
            t_w_converging = False
            error = max value
            WHILE  t_w_converging = False
                Solve for h_g using Bartz and t_w_guess
                Solve for equivalent heat flux q1 from Taw and Tco
                Solve for Tw from gas-wall convection (q1 = q2)
                IF T_sat >= Tw
                    Solve q3 from nucleate
                ELSE
                    Solve q3 from resistance
                error = q1 - q3
                IF abs(error) > tol (set tol)
                    New t_w_guess from secant
                ELSE
                    t_w_converging = true
    
            CHF CHECK
            Solve wall-coolant flux q"
            Find CHF with HH equations
            IF q" >= CHF
                Take channel geometry from previous iteration

            COOLANT UPDATE
            Calculate next T_co
            Calculate presure loss
            Update rho
            Update k
            Update Cp
            Update mu

    IF P_final = P_target
        Return
    ELSE
        New P_guess with secant

(stress analysis)
IF stress analysis passes
    Increase channel height
ELSE
    Take channel geometry from previous iteration
    Script ends

(if script fails on first run, smth def wrong; scrip